  "prefLabel": "Lab 205.05 Motions",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Lab 205.05 Motions.\n\n(a) All dispositive motions, motions to exclude disclosed evidence, and motions challenging jurisdiction or raising procedural matters shall be filed in accordance with Lab 203.06 in triplicate.\n\n(b) If a motion is filed after a date is assigned for the compensation appeals board hearing, the motion shall be heard at the onset of the scheduled appeal and, if appropriate, the hearing shall go forward on the merits.\n\nSource. #8922-A, eff 7-1-07; ss by #14534, eff 3-12-26",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/lab200.html"
